  "rootCauseEvidence": "the configured task exited 1 three times on '\"DB_HOST\" Environment Variable is missing' (CONTAINER_START_FAILED via the DEPLOY-011 crash-loop rule). The manifest bound only the standard DATABASE_* names: the analyser's env-var model held two variables for the whole repository because directus reads configuration through a local env object (const env = useEnv(); env['DB_HOST'] in api/src/database/index.ts, a file the analyser had fetched) and every JS/TS recogniser keyed on process.env — so no DB_* alias and no minted KEY/SECRET (unboundSecretKeys: ADMIN_PASSWORD, KEY, SECRET). Second shape of DEPLOY-005; generic fix PR #224 (analysis v17). Everything before the task start passed: zero-task INSTALL, CONFIG_UPDATE, release scale-up. Observation: a template-revision task booted on SQLite for ~5 min next to the configured revision before the rollout replaced it.",
  "findingIds": [
    "DEPLOY-005"
  ],
